[00:07.27] Night: her sable dome scattered with diamonds
[00:10.76] Fused my dust from a light year
[00:15.70] Squeezed me to her breast, sowed me with carbon
[00:19.48] Strung my warp across time
[00:24.53] Gave me each a horse, sunrise and graveyard
[00:28.07] Told me only I was her
[00:31.41] Bid me face the east closed me in questions
[00:34.88] Built the sky for my dawn
[00:38.23]
[00:55.38] Cleaned my feet of mud, followed the empty
[00:58.61] Zebra ride to the cirkus
[01:03.67] Past a painted cage, spoke to the paybox
[01:06.90] Glove which wrote on my tongue
[01:12.06] Pushed me down a slide to the arena
[01:15.44] Megaphonium fanfare
[01:18.76] In his cloak of words strode the ringmaster
[01:22.08] Bid me join the parade
[01:26.09]
[01:54.87] "Worship!" Cried the clown, "I'm a TV"
[01:58.04] "Making bandsmen go clockwork"
[02:02.88] "See the slinky seal cirkus policeman"
[02:06.37] "Bareback ladies have fish"
[02:11.09] Strongmen by his feet, plate-spinning statesman
[02:14.74] Accrobatically juggling
[02:18.03] Bids his tamers go quiet the tumblers
[02:21.28] Lest the mirror stop turning
[02:25.04]
[03:21.17] Elephants forgot, force-fed on stale chalk
[03:24.43] Ate the floors of their cages
[03:29.08] Strongmen lost their hair, paybox collapsed and
[03:32.42] Lions sharpened their teeth
[03:37.26] Gloves raced round the ring, stallions stampeded
[03:40.40] Pandemonium seesaw
[03:43.57] I ran for the door, ringmaster shouted
[03:46.84] "All the fun of the cirkus!"
[03:50.27]